($t$Piper nigrum$t$, $t$Piper nigrum$t$, $t$Piperaceae$t$, $t$Famiglia botanica: Piperaceae. Portamento: Climber. Altezza massima indicativa: 6 m. Piper nigrum or commonly known as Black Pepper is a perennial flowering woody vine growing about 8-10 m long and commonly found in East Asia. The leaves are thick and leathery, and arranged alternately. It is widely cultivated for its fruits, known as peppercorns, which are usually dried then ground into powder and used as a spice and food flavoring. The fruits lower fever, improve digestion, and can be used as disinfectant. The seeds, on the other hand, is used for indigestion, food poisoning, cholera, diarrhea, dysentery, vomiting caused by cold, nasal congestion, sinusitis, epilepsy, and inflammation of the skin. The essential oil is used for rheumatic pain and toothache. It is also used in perfumery and as food flavoring.$t$, $j${"luce": "Mezz'ombra", "acqua": "Moderata", "terreno": "Tollera terreno: sabbioso/leggero, medio, argilloso/pesante"}$j$::jsonb, ARRAY[$t$Scheda in bozza, importata automaticamente da Plants For A Future (pfaf.org): dati non verificati manualmente, da controllare prima di considerarli affidabili$t$, $t$Nome comune (inglese, fonte PFAF): Black Pepper$t$, $t$Rischi segnalati dalla fonte (testo originale in inglese, non tradotto per non alterarne il significato): None known$t$], $j${"irrigazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "concimazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "potatura": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "npk": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}}$j$::jsonb, $j${"famiglia_botanica": "Piperaceae", "giorni_germinazione": null, "giorni_trapianto": null, "giorni_raccolta": null, "finestra_semina": [], "finestra_trapianto": [], "resistenza_gelo": "bassa", "spaziatura_cm": null, "consociazioni_favorevoli": [], "consociazioni_sfavorevoli": 